// facet_gtk test root. Importing is what compiles a module into the gate, so
// every module is imported here whether or not this file names it again.
//
// ---- what can be asserted here, and what cannot -------------------------------
//
// NOTHING IN THIS FILE MAKES A WIDGET. `gtk_init` needs a display, and a suite
// that only runs where someone is logged in is a suite that stops running. So
// what is pinned here is everything the backend DECIDES — the mappings, the
// CSS it composes, the bits it claims, the encoders — and nothing that needs
// GTK to be up.
//
// The other half is `examples/facet_gtk_probe`, and it is an APP on purpose:
// whether the switch reported its change, whether the slider fired while it was
// being dragged, whether the field kept its caret — none of that is assertable
// by a process with no hands. The division is the repo's standing rule: pin the
// state machine in a test, then hand a human a probe.
//
// This file is skipped by `tools/parity.py`, which is why the coverage number
// is not inflated by a test naming a prop bit.

